  "language_probability": 1,
  "text": "Place an object on this digital scale and its weight appears as a number. Inside, the platform bends a tiny metal element by an extremely small amount. That element is a load cell, built to deform predictably under force. Thin strain gauges attach to it, stretch or compress along with the metal. Their electrical resistance changes, producing a small voltage signal. The scale's electronics amplify and convert that signal into a digital reading. Calibration relates the reading to weight units, while tear subtracts the container. So a tiny mechanical bend becomes the number you see on the scale.",
